We examine the impact of $b 	o c$ measurements on the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay within the $U_1$ leptoquark model. The $U_1$ leptoquark model is capable of explaining the $R_{D^{(*)}}$ and $R_{K^{(*)}}$ anomalies, and we find that the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay is significantly influenced by the $b 	o c$ measurements. The $b 	o c$ measurements can be used to constrain the $U_1$ leptoquark model, and we find that the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay is in good agreement with the experimental data.
